@startuml
title The interaction cut, instantiated: from Milner's factoring, through Pi's `Comm` clause, to the generated patterns

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #6D28D9
  FontColor #111827
}

package "LAYER 1 — the schema (†): two introductions meet along matching surfaces" as L1 #F8FAFC {
  rectangle "**interaction constructor** <latex>K</latex>\nbrings two operands into contact" as T_K #DBEAFE
  rectangle "**program introduction** <latex>K_p(I, C_p)</latex>\nsurface <latex>I</latex> + program continuation <latex>C_p</latex>" as T_KP #DCFCE7
  rectangle "**environment introduction** <latex>K_e(J, C_e)</latex>\nsurface <latex>J</latex> + environment continuation <latex>C_e</latex>" as T_KE #FEF3C7
  rectangle "**contraction** <latex>\mathrm{compute}(I, J, C_p, C_e)</latex>\npartial — defined only when the surfaces match" as T_C #FCE7F3
}

package "LAYER 2 — the Pi clause that instantiates it" as L2 #F8FAFC {
  rectangle "<latex>K = </latex> **PPar**\nan AC bag: ""ps:HashBag(Proc)""" as P_K #DBEAFE
  rectangle "<latex>K_p = </latex> **PIn**\nsurface = the subject ""n"";\ncontinuation = the abstraction <latex>\lambda x.p</latex>" as P_KP #DCFCE7
  rectangle "<latex>K_e = </latex> **POut**\nsurface = the subject ""n"";\ncontinuations = the pair <latex>(m, q)</latex>" as P_KE #FEF3C7
  rectangle "contraction = **pseudo-application**\n<latex>p\{m/x\} \;\mid\; q</latex>\nwritten ""(eval ^x.p m)"" and ""q"" in the reduct bag" as P_C #FCE7F3
}

package "LAYER 3 — the generated data that executes it" as L3 #F8FAFC {
  rectangle """Pattern::ac(PiDovetailOp::Proc_PPar, [...], Some(\"rest\"))""\nthe AcApp whose remainder absorbs every non-participant" as G_K #DBEAFE
  rectangle "**element 0** — ""Pattern::app(Proc_PIn,""\n""  [var(n), leaf(BinderArity(1)), var(p)])""" as G_KP #DCFCE7
  rectangle "**element 1** — ""Pattern::app(Proc_POut,""\n""  [var(n), var(m), var(q)])""" as G_KE #FEF3C7
  rectangle "**op 0 dispatch arm**\n""open_body.substitute_name(&b.0, &arg)""\nspliced as ""[var(__comm_reduct), var(q)]""" as G_C #FCE7F3
}

T_K -[#1D4ED8,thickness=2]-> P_K
T_KP -[#15803D,thickness=2]-> P_KP
T_KE -[#B45309,thickness=2]-> P_KE
T_C -[#BE185D,thickness=2]-> P_C

P_K -[#1D4ED8,thickness=2]-> G_K
P_KP -[#15803D,thickness=2]-> G_KP
P_KE -[#B45309,thickness=2]-> G_KE
P_C -[#BE185D,thickness=2]-> G_C

note right of T_C #EDE9FE
  <latex>\dfrac{(C_p', C_e') = \mathrm{compute}(I, J, C_p, C_e)}{K(K_p(I, C_p),\, K_e(J, C_e)) \longrightarrow K'(C_p', C_e')}</latex>
end note

note right of P_KE #FEE2E2
  **The surface match is the only guard.**
  Because ""n"" occurs in BOTH elements, the AC
  matcher's re-bind check enforces <latex>n \equiv n</latex> by
  e-class equality. An input on ""c"" and an
  output on ""d"" therefore produce no match
  and no firing — the term simply rests.
end note

note right of G_C #DCFCE7
  **Binding is not the point.** Pseudo-application
  factors into the substitution <latex>p\{m/x\}</latex> — by which a
  datum migrates through a binder — and the release
  of the environment's residual <latex>q</latex>. Pi's asynchronous
  ""CommAsync"" has the same cut with an EMPTY release,
  so its reduct is the arity-1 ""[var(__comm_reduct)]"".
end note

legend right
|= Colour |= Role across all three layers |
|<#DBEAFE> blue | the interaction constructor — where contact happens |
|<#DCFCE7> green | the program side: the receive, its subject and its abstraction |
|<#FEF3C7> amber | the environment side: the send, its subject and its objects |
|<#FCE7F3> pink | the contraction that combines the two continuations |
endlegend

@enduml
